  data: {
    LLM: "1. The Pitch: The player to the dealer's left leads a card. The suit of this card is the trump suit.\n2. Trick Play: Players must follow suit if possible. In strict All Fours tradition, some leagues allow 'playing a trump' even if you have the led suit.\n3. Card Ranking: A (high) K, Q, J, 10, 9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2.",
    Player: "1. The Pitch: The player to the dealer's left leads a card. The suit of this card is the trump suit.\n2. Trick Play: Players must follow suit if possible. In strict All Fours tradition, some leagues allow 'playing a trump' even if you have the led suit.\n3. Card Ranking: A (high) K, Q, J, 10, 9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2.",
    objective: "Reach 121 points by capturing scoring cards and winning the 'Game' point.",
    gameplay: "1. The Pitch: The player to the dealer's left leads a card. The suit of this card is the trump suit.\n2. Trick Play: Players must follow suit if possible. In strict All Fours tradition, some leagues allow 'playing a trump' even if you have the led suit.\n3. Card Ranking: A (high) K, Q, J, 10, 9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2.",
    keyRules: [
      "Only the 36 dealt cards are scored for the 'Game' point.",
      "Fives are often called 'Don cards' or 'Pedros'.",
      "Winning the 'Low' point requires tracking the lowest trump seen in play.",
